1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Policies get careful prose review, but they rarely get the equivalent of unit tests.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:20,000
PolicyFuzz explores a narrow test-and-evaluation question: can a reviewer turn policy intent into cited, executable scenarios, expose a concrete gap or conflict, and retest a confirmed revision without handing judgment to a model?

3
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:28,333
Our working user is a Finance or People Ops reviewer.

4
00:00:28,333 --> 00:00:36,667
The problem statement is still a hypothesis, not validated market research: edge cases span thresholds, exceptions, and interacting clauses, while a manual pass gives little reusable regression evidence.

5
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:45,000
The two bounded manual-review exercises are still pending, so this rehearsal makes no speed or customer claim.

6
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:51,250
In the final take, we will upload the synthetic policy on the frozen build.

7
00:00:51,250 --> 00:00:57,500
Proposed rules retain source citations, and unsupported language stays visible instead of being silently normalized.

8
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:03,750
The reviewer checks the structured contract and explicitly confirms it before generation can continue.

9
00:01:03,750 --> 00:01:10,000
This pause is the first trust boundary: interpretation is proposed by a model; authority stays with the reviewer and deterministic validators.

10
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,500
The current public cached rehearsal record has exactly three deterministic baseline findings.

11
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:25,000
First is a receipt-requirement finding.

12
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:32,500
In the final capture, we select its exact witness and open the cited rule, resolved values, and deterministic trace.

13
00:01:32,500 --> 00:01:40,000
Second is an approval-requirement finding.

14
00:01:40,000 --> 00:01:47,500
The final narration must follow the displayed witness and citations; it must not imply that the system resolved legal meaning.

15
00:01:47,500 --> 00:01:55,000
Third is a daily-category-cap finding.

16
00:01:55,000 --> 00:02:02,500
We will show the scenario inputs, the invariant witness, and the trace that connects the observed behavior to the reviewer-confirmed intent.

17
00:02:02,500 --> 00:02:10,000
All three are accepted by authored demonstration decisions in the cached record.

18
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:17,500
That proves a reproducible rehearsal path, not independent human review or blind benchmark eligibility.

19
00:02:17,500 --> 00:02:25,000
Final narration may call them frozen results only when the Gate B evidence and capture show the same witnesses, traces, citations, and one-to-one matches.

20
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:29,167
The current cached run accepted 10 scenarios.

21
00:02:29,167 --> 00:02:33,333
Its initial provisional suite already satisfied the configured minimum: all 10 rules and all three invariants were covered, with 23 of 26 predicate branches covered.

22
00:02:33,333 --> 00:02:37,500
The recorded targeted_cycles value is zero, so the workflow froze the suite without an adaptive model call.

23
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:41,667
One targeted cycle remains available only when minimum coverage is missing.

24
00:02:41,667 --> 00:02:45,833
The rehearsal must not stage a fake adaptive cycle.

25
00:02:45,833 --> 00:02:50,000
Final development recall remains unstated until frozen benchmark evidence exists.

26
00:02:50,000 --> 00:02:57,000
PolicyFuzz pauses again.

27
00:02:57,000 --> 00:03:04,000
Candidate findings cannot be accepted, and structural findings need reviewer severity.

28
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:11,000
In the current cached rehearsal, authored demonstration decisions accept the three supported findings and produce a three-operation revision proposal.

29
00:03:11,000 --> 00:03:18,000
Nothing is published automatically.

30
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:25,000
The revision is applied only after session confirmation, and that confirmation event must be visible in the final capture.

31
00:03:25,000 --> 00:03:32,500
After confirmation, deterministic Python reruns the identical frozen suite.

32
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:40,000
In the current cached rehearsal, findings move from three to zero, all 12 previously inconclusive assertions pass, and every patch-acceptance gate is true: suite identity, target fixes, failures outside targets, protected cases, newly bad states, unrelated-rule signatures, and holdout deterioration.

33
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:47,500
The final capture must still show the same suite hash before and after.

34
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:55,000
Frozen development regression remains unstated until final evidence exists.

35
00:03:55,000 --> 00:04:01,250
Models interpret language, generate bounded tests, and draft a proposal.

36
00:04:01,250 --> 00:04:07,500
They do not assign authoritative verdicts, severity, scored answers, hashes, or patch acceptance.

37
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:13,750
Deterministic code owns those decisions.

38
00:04:13,750 --> 00:04:20,000
Human confirmation gates contract acceptance, finding decisions, and revision application; the public view excludes prompts, credentials, and full uploaded text.

39
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:25,000
The current public cached rehearsal contains 10 scenarios, three accepted finding decisions, four scripted model responses, and zero actual provider calls.

40
00:04:25,000 --> 00:04:30,000
It is synthetic, cached, and blind-scoring-ineligible.

41
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:35,000
Confirmation count, elapsed run time, provider cost, manual-review comparisons, and the blind score remain unstated until their required frozen or human evidence exists.

42
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:40,000
PolicyFuzz offers review coverage and repeatable regression evidence; it does not prove compliance or exhaustive discovery.
